    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0b7a8272b583491aafcacf8367a09d16",
      "statement": "UNSEARCHABLE_TRUST names untrusted and no_text in one place because three components need the identical rule — lookup excludes those pages from hits, verify reports unverifiable for them, and the observed-token inventory takes no codes from them — while degraded is deliberately excluded as a text layer with problems rather than one that cannot be read.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/core/record.py#L43-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e8ad24790726d8152bc55684f7255cd7238c542a657374d0d79f603ed4dda694:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d9f18301b3443678abb9b8cb8f5cc76",
      "statement": "blind_spot marks a document whose searchable ratio is zero, because such a binder has no text surface for a query carrying a printed code to reach and would otherwise leave the answer set silently — whereas a partially scanned document is still found through the pages that do have text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/core/health.py#L136-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:da6be4f10644740f63104dbca503531bdab8f74fb742b0c2db138ca37ef7d62a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_394186cdb8d34cc6b460c09d5d9058ac",
      "statement": "demote ensures a page is never more trusted than its document, because filtering and verification act per page and a document-level signal nothing on a page reflects would have no effect; no_text is never overwritten, since why that page is unsearchable is a fact about the page rather than the document.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/vsir/core/health.py#L207-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d44746f12ecd7b93649e00a330a599d40c13209524edf65e9cf9b5b10eb9b30:"
        }
